---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{#
  layouts/workspace.njk
  ---------------------
  The workspace picture, filling the whole window. It is 60 pictures taken as
  a camera pans across the scene in Blender (assets/img/workspace/0001.webp
  to 0060.webp); assets/js/workspace.js shows the one that matches where the
  mouse is, so moving the mouse left and right looks around the room.

  Settings on the canvas:
        data-frames   how many pictures there are
        data-path     the folder they are in
        data-ext      their file type (webp, jpg...)
        data-invert   "true" to flip the direction
#}
<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ title }}</h1>

<canvas class="ws" data-workspace
        data-frames="60"
        data-path="{{ '/assets/img/workspace/' | url }}"
        data-ext="webp"
        data-invert="false"
        role="img"
        aria-label="An interactive view of the workspace. Move the mouse left and right to look around."></canvas>
<p class="ws__status" data-workspace-status aria-live="polite"></p>
